dmrcrack (0.5.2+dfsg-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream releases 0.5.1 and 0.5.2.
  * Fix the wrong Message Indicator on multi-transmission (repeater) captures,
    the main cause of "finds nothing on a real capture": each burst now maps to
    the Privacy Indicator of its own call, and the MI is back-extrapolated when
    voice is decoded before the first clean PI header.
  * Fix the GPU never running on the CLI default: "--samples 0" (use all
    payloads) left the per-device payload limit at 0, so every GPU worker bailed
    and the scan fell back to CPU-only scoring.
  * Fix a heap overflow when staging payloads for the legacy kernel on captures
    beyond ~249 bursts (most multi-minute recordings).
  * Classify ALG 0x26 (Caltta Basic Privacy) as unsupported instead of starting
    a scan it cannot win; only ALG 0x02 is Hytera Enhanced Privacy.
  * Stop over-tagging silence frames so the KPA pre-filter no longer discards the
    correct key on layouts that emit a per-burst CACH marker.

 -- Felix Sasian Pacheco <sasianfelix@gmail.com>  Tue, 14 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

dmrcrack (0.5.0+dfsg-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Re-derive the per-burst detection floor so a noisy real-world capture no
    longer prunes the correct key; wrong keys are still rejected within a
    superframe.
  * Report a CONFIRMED / UNVERIFIED / no-key verdict instead of a raw score, so
    a dictionary or statistical latch is never presented as a recovered key.
  * Hytera Enhanced Privacy: build the RC4 keystream once per key instead of
    once per superframe (about 3.4x faster), and advance the inter-superframe
    MI with its own LFSR so one decoded PI header tags a whole capture.
  * Recognise Hytera Enhanced Privacy under both ALG 0x02 and 0x26.
  * Report a GPU backend failure as an error instead of a misleading
    "interrupted" result.
  * Add native sm_120 (RTX 50-series) SASS instead of relying on PTX JIT.

 -- Felix Sasian Pacheco <sasianfelix@gmail.com>  Mon, 27 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000

dmrcrack (0.4.1+dfsg-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Report the closest candidate (its per-burst Hamming rate and how many bursts
    it survived) when a full scan finds no key above the recovery threshold,
    instead of a bare "best candidate 0.00".
  * Only present a recovered key when the score clears the noise floor; a run
    that recovers nothing now reports "No key above the recovery threshold".
  * Windows GUI: add a taskbar progress indicator and an NVML-based GPU
    temperature read-out with a configurable thermal auto-pause.
  * Fix a stale comment describing the superseded byte-aligned Hytera keystream
    model (it is consumed as a 49-bit bitstream).

 -- Felix Sasian Pacheco <sasianfelix@gmail.com>  Thu, 18 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000

dmrcrack (0.4.0+dfsg-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 0.4.0.
  * Refuse to brute-force unsupported ciphers (AES): the engine now classifies
    the capture up front and aborts on non-RC4 traffic instead of running a full
    keyspace scan and reporting a junk key.
  * Fix an out-of-bounds read in precompute_cipher_packs on payloads shorter
    than 33 bytes (CPU and OpenCL host paths).
  * Single-source the DMR de-interleave tables in include/dmr_tables.h.

 -- Felix Sasian Pacheco <sasianfelix@gmail.com>  Tue, 09 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000

dmrcrack (0.3.3+dfsg-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian package.
  * Build the portable CPU-only engine (no CUDA/HIP build dependency) so the
    package builds with a free toolchain on the Debian/Kali autobuilders.
  * Repack the upstream tarball (+dfsg) to drop the prebuilt Windows-only
    WinSparkle binaries (see debian/copyright Files-Excluded).

